The Bluestock Mutual Fund Capstone Project is designed to collect and analyze mutual fund data from different sources. In this project, multiple datasets are loaded and explored using Python and Pandas. Live NAV data is fetched using the MFAPI service, and data quality checks are performed to identify missing values and inconsistencies. The project also validates AMFI scheme codes and organizes all files in a structured folder system. Git and GitHub are used for version control, making the project easy to manage and update.
